  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to SSCC Annual Activities.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The South Sudan Council of Churches is an ecumenical body of seven members churches and associate members that was created in July 2013 with a mission to convene civic education, advocacy, peace and reconciliation, Relief and Development services. 
Following the end of the General Secretary term of service, transition leadership was formed for 6 months and plan to conduct a general assembly was agreed upon in Mombasa retreat so that election for a new leadership would take place during the 2nd General Assembly. 
The 2nd General Assembly for the South Sudan Council of Churches will take place on 2nd -7th Dec 2024 in Peace Sheppard Centre, Kit, South Sudan, Under the theme; Building the Church. It is a crucial event that provides an opportunity for reflection on the church&apos;s progress, spiritual nourishment and strategic planning for future activities.</narrative>
  </description>
